        <h3>Raffles close at sellout or authorized stop.</h3>
        <p>A raffle does not close casually. It closes when inventory is exhausted or an authorized admin stops it for a valid, logged reason.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="kicker">Lock rule</p>
        <h3>Sellout creates a locked state.</h3>
        <p>Once sold out, the raffle is marked closed and the purchase flow stops accepting additional entries.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="kicker">Draw rule</p>
        <h3>Immediate or scheduled mode must be visible.</h3>
        <p>Each raffle should say whether it draws immediately after sellout or moves into the next public event slot.</p>
